From: ficciones
Subject: focusing a window arms the gradient-angle loop

Hyprland 0.57.1 attaches the loop's end callback only in onWindowMap, and only when the angle
animation is enabled at that moment. A window mapped before a reload turned the loop on spins
one turn per focus and stops. onWindowFocus now arms the same callback.

--- a/src/render/decorations/AnimatedDecorationGradient.cpp
+++ b/src/render/decorations/AnimatedDecorationGradient.cpp
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@
 
     m_angleProgress->setValueAndWarp(0.F);
     *m_angleProgress = 1.F;
+    // a window mapped before a reload turned the loop on never got the callback onWindowMap arms
+    m_angleProgress->setCallbackOnEnd([this](WP<CBaseAnimatedVariable> animation) { onAngleAnimationEnd(animation); }, false);
 }
 
 void CAnimatedDecorationGradient::onAngleAnimationEnd(WP<CBaseAnimatedVariable> animation) {
